            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life and Education of Ken Thompson</strong><br>\nKen Thompson was born in 1943 in New Orleans, Louisiana. From an early age, he showed an interest in electronics and programming. He attended the University of California at Berkeley where he earned his Bachelor's degree in Electrical Engineering and Master's degree in Electrical Engineering and Computer Science. His studies laid the foundation for his contributions to computer science and his later work on the UNIX operating system.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Beginnings at Bell Labs</strong><br>\nAfter completing his education, Ken Thompson began working at Bell Labs. It was here that he, along with colleague Dennis Ritchie, began the development of the UNIX operating system. Bell Labs provided an environment that encouraged innovation and the exploration of new ideas, which was instrumental in the creation of UNIX.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Development of UNIX</strong><br>\nThe development of UNIX began in the late 1960s when Thompson and Ritchie sought to create a more flexible and portable operating system. UNIX was revolutionary in that it was written in the C programming language, which allowed it to be installed on many different types of hardware. This made UNIX incredibly versatile and widely adopted.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
