      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Contributions to Programming Languages</strong><br>\nKen Thompson is not only known for his work on UNIX but also for his contributions to programming languages. He was involved in the creation of the B programming language, which was a precursor to the C language. His work on these languages has had a lasting impact on software development and programming.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Creation of Other Tools</strong><br>\nBeyond UNIX and programming languages, Thompson created several other important tools and software. He developed regular expression notation, which is used to specify search patterns in text processing. He also helped create the UTF-8 encoding, a character encoding that enabled the consistent representation and handling of text expressed in most of the world's writing systems.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Collaborative Work with Dennis Ritchie</strong><br>\nKen Thompson's collaboration with Dennis Ritchie was a defining factor in his career. Together, they achieved many technological breakthroughs. Their joint efforts were recognized when they were awarded the Turing Award in 1983 for their contributions to the development of operating systems, specifically UNIX, which had by then become synonymous with robust and flexible software design.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
